# Project overview

White-label, multi-tenant blogging platform (DataMoon internship project).
Each tenant gets its own blog on its own subdomain and its own MySQL database.

## Stack (pinned)
- Laravel 11
- stancl/tenancy ^3.8, database-per-tenant (MySQL), tenants identified by domain
- Central app: `blogs.test`; tenant blogs: `<name>.blogs.test` (e.g. `acme.blogs.test`)
- Served locally by Laravel Herd
- Frontend: React via Inertia (Laravel Breeze)
- Tests: PHPUnit

## Hard rules
- Do NOT upgrade Laravel or stancl/tenancy, including major or minor version bumps in composer.json.
- Do NOT add any dependency (composer or npm) without asking first and explaining why.
- Prefer built-in Laravel and stancl/tenancy features over new packages.
- See `tenancy.mdc`, `frontend.mdc` and `git-workflow.mdc` for area-specific rules.
